# The z-axis layout: every path the tooling uses outside the z-axis checkout, in one place.
# Read by paths.sh (shell: source it) and zpaths.py (Python), and by tools/readable/zaxis_paths.py
# in z-axis. A name already set in the environment wins over its line here. Values may use $HOME (the user's own
# home from the password database, or ZAXIS_HOME: never the environment's HOME, so a scratch HOME finds the data) and
# names defined above them. One NAME=VALUE per line; comments on their own lines.
#
# These are the defaults: data, scratch and discs beside the checkout. A workshop's own layout goes in
# workshop/merge/paths.env (read first, so its names win over these; the environment wins over both).
#
# ZAXIS_MAIN, the main checkout (merges, its build dirs, the workspaces below), is found by git from
# wherever a tool runs (a worktree's main checkout); this line is the fallback when git finds none.
ZAXIS_MAIN=$HOME/Developer/z-axis
# Lanes' worktrees: one per agent, inside the main checkout so CLAUDE.md applies to them.
ZAXIS_WORKTREES=$ZAXIS_MAIN/wt
# Everything that is never committed: generated code, disc files, dumps, saves, apps, screenshots.
ZAXIS_DATA=$ZAXIS_MAIN-data
AI_DATA=$ZAXIS_DATA/ai
DM2_DATA=$ZAXIS_DATA/dm2
XBOX_DATA=$ZAXIS_DATA/xbox
# The games' folders in the tree in use (ZAXIS: the checkout this tools/ folder is in, or the copy a job runs): each
# game's workspace (recomp, ghidra, decomp, and the data links into AI_DATA and DM2_DATA that setup.sh makes from
# setup/data-links.txt) and its own tools. A lane's copy runs its own scripts, never main's (tools34: int28's gate ran
# main's run-game-dm2.sh from its copy). A copy's data links are made when first missing (paths.sh, zpaths.py: the
# same targets as main's).
AI_WORKSPACE=$ZAXIS/games/aggressive/workspace
DM2_WORKSPACE=$ZAXIS/games/dm2/workspace
BMX_WORKSPACE=$ZAXIS/games/bmx/workspace
AI_TOOLS=$ZAXIS/games/aggressive/tools
DM2_TOOLS=$ZAXIS/games/dm2/tools
BMX_TOOLS=$ZAXIS/games/bmx/tools
# The work database's tool (all games).
WORKDB_PY=$ZAXIS_TOOLING/workdb/workdb.py
# Agents' scratch: lane logs, the recording corpus, the work database, the merge scripts' and
# rcheck's output (logs, the checker pins, results, state).
ZAXIS_SCRATCH=$ZAXIS_MAIN-scratch
MERGE_OUT=$ZAXIS_SCRATCH/merge
REMOTE_OUT=$ZAXIS_SCRATCH/remote
# BMX XXX's recompiled code (recomp/generated-ns, namespace bmx) and disc copy (disc), where bmxcorpus made them
# (the BMX tools' default too: bmxroutes.py, run-game-dm2.sh GAME=bmx, playbot/bmx.py).
BMX_DATA=$ZAXIS_DATA/bmx
# BMX XXX's recompile: its generated-ns (with the VU0 upload), generated-vu1 (the VU1 micro memory image) and the
# configs they are made from, all made by BMX_WORKSPACE's recomp/recompile.py from its Ghidra export
# (recomp/config.toml), as DM2's are in DM2_WORKSPACE's recomp. Every build and tool reads BMX XXX's code here.
BMX_RECOMP=$BMX_DATA/recomp
# The set of generated code this tooling's builds use (recompiler/generated_key.py: the key of the recompiler and the
# three games' inputs): each game's folder with -<set> after its name ($AI_DATA/recomp/generated-<set>,
# $DM2_DATA/recomp/generated-ns-<set>, $BMX_RECOMP/generated-ns-<set>), made once by recompiler/make-generated.sh
# and never written again, so trees with another recompiler keep building with theirs. Empty: the plain folders (a
# recompiler from before game modules). zgen (paths.sh) and zpaths.generated() give a folder's; rcheck.py sends the set
# to the other hosts as its --gen-set. Only builds need it: the generated functions' text is the same in every set.
GENERATED_SET=
# The other games' symbol tables (dm2.tsv, bmx.tsv, each with its .layout.tsv) are a tree's own since tools39:
# tools/readable/bind, committed (readable_symbols.py bind --write, --check), the collection build's ZX_BIND_DIR.
# GAME_BIND_DIR is no name here: zpaths.py's (and paths.sh's zbind TREE) is the tree's folder ($ZAXIS_TREE, the
# checkout the working folder is in, ZAXIS_MAIN), else this one, the shared folder that commits from before tools39
# build with (never regenerated for them).
GAME_BIND_LEGACY=$ZAXIS_SCRATCH/workdb/bind
# The user's discs: read only.
GAME_DISCS=$ZAXIS_MAIN-discs
